    # Triangle AEC is a right triangle with AE = 5 and AC = 3 (radius of circle A)
    # Triangle BEC is a right triangle with BC = 8 (radius of circle B) and EC = AC + CE
    # Triangle AED is a right triangle with AD = BC - BD (since AB = AD + BD and AB = 18.3)
    # Triangle BED is a right triangle with BE = 8 and ED = BD (since CD = BD + ED and CD = x)

    # Step 2: Use the Pythagorean theorem to find the lengths of the sides of the right triangles
